Port wraps the result of strconv.Atoi with %w. strconv.ErrSyntax and strconv.ErrRange
must both be present with the two-link chain *strconv.NumError.Unwrap -> fmt.Errorf
"config: port %q: %w"; every entry must end in that fmt.Errorf link. (With the Go 1.27
stdlib, strconv.toError compares against internal/strconv constants, which the tool
cannot decide: the bare "concrete internal/strconv.Error" entries are an accepted
over-approximation, at run time every Atoi error is a *NumError.)
-- args --
config/config.go:@port
